Restore FUN_1000_4c9a's SS-relative dynamic-segment source pointer (Ghidra dropped the DS far-base).

4c9a builds a filename by copying a template from [SS:0x70]:SI into SS:0x740. The source SEGMENT is
held in the stack-segment scratch slot SS:0x70 (SS=DGROUP=0x1c00 after the CRT stack fixup); the asm
does `mov ax,ss:[0x70]; mov ds,ax; lodsb ds:[si]`. Ghidra mis-resolved ss:[0x70] to a fixed absolute
DAT_2000_bb00 (its static SS context 0x2ba9) into a dead var and dropped the `mov ds,ax`, leaving the
source as a bare `*param_1` (param_1 = the SI offset). Dereferencing the offset as a host pointer
SIGSEGVs for small offsets. Reconstruct the far read [DGROUP:0x70]:SI -> g_mem. The source segment
(DGROUP:0x70) is the engine's far string/resource data group; it is seeded to its base-0 paragraph
0x2d74 (oracle: runtime base_seg+0x2d74) by the loader role in native_main (fist_install_dgroup).
Dest SS:0x740 = 0x1c740 (Ghidra got that right, SS=DGROUP). Class: "SS-relative dynamic-segment
scratch" (docs/stage1.md), distinct from the DS=CS and seg-wrap classes.

